How It Works

Parent Process (Producer)

Asks the user to enter numbers.

Sends numbers to the child through pipe1.

Waits for confirmation from the child via pipe2.

Repeats this until it has sent MAX numbers.

Child Process (Consumer)

Waits for numbers from the parent via pipe1.

Prints each received number.

Sends back a "CONSUMED" message through pipe2.

Repeats this until all numbers are processed.

Important Constants

STR_LEN: Maximum length of messages.

MAX: Number of values to process.

Error Handling

Checks if pipes are created successfully.

Ensures fork() works properly.

Makes sure messages are properly formatted.
